      "versionNonce": 1276155043,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793430305143,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Algorithm for BFS\n-------------------------\n\n1. create an array of size equal to number of vertices, and set each\nelement with false .\n\n2. Now find the source vertex and enque it in the QUEUE .\n\n3. Repeat the following steps if the Queue is not empty :\n\n    a. Dequeue the HEAD of the Queue .\n\n    b. Check whether it is visited or not .\n\n    c. If not visited then :\n         \n             i. Print it\n            ii. Set visited entry to true .\n           iii. enque all its adjacent vertices into Queue.\n    \n    d. Goto Step a.\n\n\n4. Finish and return .\n\n\n\n\nAlgorithm for DFS\n-------------------------\n\n1. create an array of size equal to number of vertices, and set each\nelement with false .\n\n2. Now find the source vertex and push it in the STACK.\n\n3. Repeat the following steps if the STACK is not empty :\n\n    a. POP the TOP of the STACK.\n\n    b. Check whether it is visited or not .\n\n    c. If not visited then :\n         \n             i. Print it\n            ii. Set visited entry to true .\n           iii. PUSH all its adjacent vertices into STACK.\n    \n    d. Goto Step a.\n\n\n4. Finish and return .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Algorithm for BFS\n-------------------------\n\n1. create an array of size equal to number of vertices, and set each element with false .\n\n2. Now find the source vertex and enque it in the QUEUE .\n\n3. Repeat the following steps if the Queue is not empty :\n\n    a. Dequeue the HEAD of the Queue .\n\n    b. Check whether it is visited or not .\n\n    c. If not visited then :\n         \n             i. Print it\n            ii. Set visited entry to true .\n           iii. enque all its adjacent vertices into Queue.\n    \n    d. Goto Step a.\n\n\n4. Finish and return .\n\n\n\n\nAlgorithm for DFS\n-------------------------\n\n1. create an array of size equal to number of vertices, and set each element with false .\n\n2. Now find the source vertex and push it in the STACK.\n\n3. Repeat the following steps if the STACK is not empty :\n\n    a. POP the TOP of the STACK.\n\n    b. Check whether it is visited or not .\n\n    c. If not visited then :\n         \n             i. Print it\n            ii. Set visited entry to true .\n           iii. PUSH all its adjacent vertices into STACK.\n    \n    d. Goto Step a.\n\n\n4. Finish and return .",
